From: Matt Eaton <git@divinehawk.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: en8801s: make serdes polarity a board property

en8801s_phase1_init() forces both serdes lanes to normal polarity. Boards
are free to swap the differential pair to ease routing, and the MikroTik
E50UG (hEX refresh) does exactly that on ether1's receive pair.

The failure is quiet rather than obvious: an inverted K28.5 comma still
satisfies comma detection, so the SoC PCS reports RX sync and looks alive
while every decoded symbol is garbage. Clause-37 autoneg therefore never
completes, the link partner ability register stays empty and the port sits
at NO-CARRIER even though the copper side has negotiated 1G full duplex.

Read the polarity of each lane from the PHY node instead, keeping normal
on both as the default so existing boards are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Matt Eaton <git@divinehawk.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/air_en8801s.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/air_en8801s.c
@@ -255,6 +255,8 @@
 	u16 pro_version;
 	u8 pbus_addr;
 	bool pbus_addr_from_firmware;
+	bool rx_polarity_reverse;
+	bool tx_polarity_reverse;
 	bool leds_initialized;
 	unsigned long led_rules[EN8801S_LEDS];
 	enum en8801s_led_control led_control[EN8801S_LEDS];
@@ -1088,7 +1090,12 @@
 		return err;
 
 	mdelay(500);
-	pbus_data = (pbus_data & ~BIT(2)) | EN8801S_RX_POLARITY_NORMAL | EN8801S_TX_POLARITY_NORMAL;
+	pbus_data &= ~(BIT(2) | EN8801S_RX_POLARITY_NORMAL |
+		       EN8801S_TX_POLARITY_REVERSE);
+	if (!priv->rx_polarity_reverse)
+		pbus_data |= EN8801S_RX_POLARITY_NORMAL;
+	if (priv->tx_polarity_reverse)
+		pbus_data |= EN8801S_TX_POLARITY_REVERSE;
 	err = airoha_pbus_write(mbus, pbus_addr, EN8801S_RG_LTR_CTL, pbus_data);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
@@ -1705,6 +1712,10 @@
 	priv->dev = dev;
 	priv->pbus_addr = pbus_addr;
 	priv->pbus_addr_from_firmware = pbus_addr_from_firmware;
+	priv->rx_polarity_reverse =
+		device_property_read_bool(dev, "airoha,rx-polarity-reverse");
+	priv->tx_polarity_reverse =
+		device_property_read_bool(dev, "airoha,tx-polarity-reverse");
 
 	if (mdiodev->reset_gpio) {
 		dev_dbg(dev, "Assert PHY %lx HWRST until phy_init_hw", phy_addr);
